---
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import Search from '../components/Search.astro';
import exampleSource from '../../examples/system.xdl.yaml?raw';
import '../styles/home.css';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const doc = (path = '') => `${base}docs/${path}`;
const example = exampleSource.trim();
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="X-Verse is an open source platform for describing cyber-physical systems, connecting their realizations, and understanding experiment evidence." />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0e171f" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href={`${base}favicon.svg`} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={new URL(base, Astro.site)} />
    <title>X-Verse — From system description to experiment evidence</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="site-header wrap">
      <a class="wordmark" href={base} aria-label="X-Verse home"><img src={`${base}favicon.svg`} alt="" width="32" height="32" />X-VERSE<span class="wordmark-dot">/</span></a>
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a href={doc()}>Documentation</a>
        <a class="wide-nav" href={doc('concepts/architecture/')}>Architecture</a>
        <a class="wide-nav" href={doc('reference/')}>API reference</a>
      </nav>
      <a class="github-link" href="https://github.com/The-Xverse/xverse-platform">GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </header>
    <main id="main">
      <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <a class="release-tag" href={doc('status/')}><span class="status-dot"></span> OPEN SOURCE · LITE 1.0 RC.1 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <h1 id="hero-title">One system.<br />Many realities.<br /><span>Connected.</span></h1>
          <p class="hero-intro">Describe cyber-physical systems. Choose how their components are realized. Build experiments around explicit contracts and evidence.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href={doc('getting-started/first-system/')}>Start building <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="button secondary" href={doc('concepts/architecture/')}>Explore the architecture</a></div>
          <p class="hero-note">Domain-neutral by design. Apache 2.0 licensed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="system-visual" aria-label="Illustration of a logical system with selectable deployment realization">
          <div class="visual-top"><span class="mono">SYSTEM / SENSOR LOOP</span><span class="visual-live">ILLUSTRATIVE MODEL</span></div>
          <div class="diagram-grid">
            <div class="diagram-label mono">LOGICAL SYSTEM</div>
            <div class="nodes"><div class="node"><span class="node-icon" aria-hidden="true">◉</span><strong>Sensor</strong><small>observe</small></div><span class="connector" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="node controller"><span class="node-icon" aria-hidden="true">⌘</span><strong>Controller</strong><small>decide</small></div><span class="connector" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="node"><span class="node-icon" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><strong>Actuator</strong><small>act</small></div></div>
            <div class="binding-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
            <div class="realization"><span class="mono">DEPLOYMENT BINDING</span><strong id="realization-title">Simulated realization</strong><p id="realization-description" aria-live="polite">The same logical identities, bound to simulated components.</p></div>
            <div class="realization-switch" role="group" aria-label="Illustrative deployment realization"><button aria-pressed="true" data-realization="simulated">Simulation</button><button aria-pressed="false" data-realization="physical">Physical</button><button aria-pressed="false" data-realization="hybrid">Hybrid</button></div>
          </div>
          <div class="visual-footer"><span><i></i>Identity stays stable</span><span class="mono">XDL → DEPLOYMENT</span></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="principles-strip"><div class="wrap strip-inner"><span>DESCRIBE ONCE.</span><p>Logical identity <span>≠</span> physical realization</p><span>EXPERIMENT EXPLICITLY.</span></div></div>

      <section class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="architecture-title">
        <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">01 / THE PLATFORM</span><h2 id="architecture-title">A shared language.<br />Clear responsibilities.</h2></div><p>From system intent to evidence, each part has a defined boundary. Use the tools available today while the platform evolves.</p></div>
        <div class="platform-grid">
          <a class="platform-item" href={doc('guides/xdl/')}><span class="module-code">[ XDL ]</span><h3>Describe</h3><p>Model components, systems, deployments, scenarios, and profiles in canonical YAML or JSON.</p><span class="module-footer">Definition language <span>↗</span></span></a>
          <a class="platform-item" href={doc('guides/maestro/')}><span class="module-code">[ MAESTRO ]</span><h3>Coordinate</h3><p>Declare lifecycle intent and explore the bounded orchestration provided by Maestro Lite.</p><span class="module-footer">Orchestration <span>↗</span></span></a>
          <a class="platform-item" href={doc('guides/xcom/')}><span class="module-code">[ X-COM ]</span><h3>Communicate</h3><p>Connect through explicit communication contracts, observation, and controlled stimulation.</p><span class="module-footer">Communication <span>↗</span></span></a>
          <a class="platform-item" href={doc('guides/argus/')}><span class="module-code">[ ARGUS ]</span><h3>Understand</h3><p>Store and inspect bounded run evidence with Argus Lite’s offline verification and export tools.</p><span class="module-footer">Evidence & observability <span>↗</span></span></a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="example-section" aria-labelledby="example-title"><div class="wrap example-layout">
        <div class="example-copy"><span class="eyebrow">02 / START WITH INTENT</span><h2 id="example-title">Make your system<br />explicit.</h2><p>A system description records what exists and how elements relate. A deployment selects a realization. A scenario describes the experiment.</p><p>This minimal System illustrates XDL’s structure. The getting-started guide validates a complete five-resource example.</p><a class="text-link" href={doc('getting-started/first-system/')}>Walk through your first system <span>→</span></a><div class="terminal"><div class="terminal-label mono">CHECK YOUR DESCRIPTION</div><div class="terminal-command"><code>uv run --frozen xdl validate …</code><button aria-label="Copy XDL help command" data-copy="uv run --frozen xdl validate --help">Copy help</button></div><span class="terminal-output">Static validation. Explicit diagnostics.</span></div></div>
        <div class="code-window"><div class="code-title"><span><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="mono">system.xdl.yaml</span><span class="code-label">XDL v1alpha1</span></div><Code code={example} lang="yaml" theme="github-dark" /></div>
      </div></section>

      <section class="section wrap paths-section" aria-labelledby="paths-title"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">03 / FIND YOUR PATH</span><h2 id="paths-title">From first steps<br />to deeper integration.</h2></div><div class="home-search"><Search /></div></div>
        <div class="path-list">
          <a href={doc('getting-started/installation/')}><span class="path-number">01</span><div><h3>Get up and running</h3><p>Install the tools, validate an example, and compile an offline experiment plan.</p></div><span class="path-arrow">↗</span></a>
          <a href={doc('concepts/architecture/')}><span class="path-number">02</span><div><h3>Understand the system</h3><p>Explore logical identities, realization bindings, profiles, and subsystem boundaries.</p></div><span class="path-arrow">↗</span></a>
          <a href={doc('reference/')}><span class="path-number">03</span><div><h3>Work with the contracts</h3><p>Browse Python and C++ APIs, schema constraints, and the current command line.</p></div><span class="path-arrow">↗</span></a>
          <a href={doc('development/contributing/')}><span class="path-number">04</span><div><h3>Build it together</h3><p>Contribute code, examples, and documentation through the same review process.</p></div><span class="path-arrow">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="closing wrap"><div><span class="eyebrow">BUILT IN THE OPEN</span><h2>Explore what exists.<br />Help shape what comes next.</h2><p>X-Verse Lite is a bounded engineering baseline. Read the current scope and limitations before choosing an integration.</p></div><a class="button primary" href={doc('status/')}>View project status <span>→</span></a></section>
    </main>
    <footer class="wrap site-footer"><a class="wordmark" href={base}>X-VERSE<span class="wordmark-dot">/</span></a><p>Open source infrastructure for cyber-physical experiments.</p><div><a href={doc()}>Docs</a><a href="https://github.com/The-Xverse/xverse-platform">GitHub ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/The-Xverse/xverse-platform/blob/main/LICENSE">Apache 2.0</a></div></footer>
    <script>
      const states = {
        simulated: ['Simulated realization', 'The same logical identities, bound to simulated components.'],
        physical: ['Physical realization', 'The same logical identities, bound to physical devices.'],
        hybrid: ['Hybrid realization', 'The same logical identities, distributed across simulated and physical components.'],
      };
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-realization]').forEach((button) => {
        button.addEventListener('click', () => {
          const value = button.dataset.realization as keyof typeof states;
          document.querySelectorAll('[data-realization]').forEach((other) => other.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(other === button)));
          document.querySelector('#realization-title')!.textContent = states[value][0];
          document.querySelector('#realization-description')!.textContent = states[value][1];
        });
      });
      document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy]')?.addEventListener('click', async (event) => {
        const button = event.currentTarget as HTMLButtonElement;
        try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(button.dataset.copy!); button.textContent = 'Copied'; }
        catch { button.textContent = 'Select command'; }
        setTimeout(() => { button.textContent = 'Copy help'; }, 2000);
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
